docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:17:The emphasis is execution, not redesign. The repo already has the core primitives. The backlog focuses on making Phase 1 and Phase 2 more explicit, more measurable, and more proof-oriented.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:23:3. Treat claim-element proof readiness as the organizing principle for both phases.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:31:| W0 | Timeline ledger and chronology handoff | P0 | Intake and evidence share one durable event-level chronology substrate |
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:33:| W2 | Proof-directed question planning | P0 | Questions are ranked by proof gain and novelty |
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:48:Make chronology a durable cross-phase object instead of a collection of summaries inferred separately in intake and evidence.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:59:- [x] add canonical `event_ledger`, `timeline_relations`, `timeline_anchors`, and `timeline_issues` state to the intake case file
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:60:- [x] update `_apply_intake_answer_to_case_file(...)` so chronology answers create or update stable event and anchor records instead of only appending free-standing facts
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:61:- [x] update `advance_to_evidence_phase(...)`, `_summarize_intake_evidence_alignment(...)`, and `_build_alignment_evidence_tasks(...)` so temporal tasks carry event IDs, relation IDs, issue IDs, and proof objectives
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:62:- [x] extend readiness and packet summaries so unresolved timeline issues and unsupported order assumptions appear as first-class blockers
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:68:- chronology blockers can be explained in terms of missing anchors, missing relations, or contradictory events rather than only packet-level temporal weakness
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:93:- [x] expand `proof_leads` with owner, availability, expected format, retrieval path, and target linkage
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:100:- a single intake answer can produce structured facts and proof leads with stable references
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:106:- `proof_leads[]` carry collection-routing fields (`owner`, `custodian`, `availability`, `expected_format`, `retrieval_path`) and target linkage (`target_claim_types`, `target_element_ids`, `target_fact_ids`, `target_links`).
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:107:- `open_items[]` are the queueable Phase 1 work list and include `blocking_level`, `next_question_strategy`, target claim/element metadata, support kind, and proof-path status.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:108:- `get_three_phase_status()` and intake review summaries preserve raw records and expose aggregate `proof_lead_collection_summary` and `open_item_summary` payloads for operators and API consumers.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:122:Make question selection optimize for proof gain, not only generic gap reduction.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:131:- [x] add expected update kind and proof-gain metadata to question candidates
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:143:- the mediator can explain what proof objective each question serves
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:148:- `question_candidates[]` and selected intake questions now carry `proof_objective`, `proof_objective_id`, `question_objective_key`, `coverage_key`, `expected_proof_gain_score`, `proof_gain_metadata`, `novelty_score`, and `novelty_metadata`.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:149:- `ranking_explanation` and `selector_signals` preserve the same proof-objective and novelty fields so UI traces, adversarial scoring, and status summaries can explain why a question was selected.
docs/INTAKE_EVIDENCE_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:151:- Intake fact/proof-lead intent snapshots preserve `proof_objective`, `proof_objective_id`, `coverage_key`, and `novelty_score`; intent summaries expose proof-objective counts and average novelty.
