docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_PLAN.md:474:The theorem layer should distinguish four kinds of temporal proof state.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_PLAN.md:476:1. Proven chronology
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_PLAN.md:477:   Facts and relations are sufficiently grounded to satisfy the legal temporal frame.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_PLAN.md:479:2. Plausible but unanchored chronology
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_PLAN.md:480:   Relative ordering exists, but the timeline still lacks enough anchoring to support proof.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_PLAN.md:482:3. Contradicted chronology
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_PLAN.md:483:   Competing evidence or mutually incompatible date claims prevent reliable proof.
docs/TEMPORAL_TIMELINE_PROOF_PLAN.md:485:4. Legally irrelevant chronology
